// Mutation testing of antevemus/aspecification-redis-streams (1.0.1): the whole src/. Runs in the scheduled
// workflow (.github/workflows/quality.yml) with a coverage driver (pcov) and a Redis 7.4 service; locally,
// against a Redis server for tests (see phpunit.xml.dist):
//
//   ASPEC_REDIS_HOST=127.0.0.1 ASPEC_REDIS_PORT=16379 XDEBUG_MODE=off vendor/bin/infection --threads=1 \
//       --only-covering-test-cases --initial-tests-php-options="-d pcov.enabled=1 -d pcov.directory=$PWD/src"
//
// Measured on 2026-11-18 (1.0.1 against ASpecification 2.15.0, whose contract battery the suite runs against
// Redis; Infection 0.35.12, PHP 8.4.27 with pcov, Redis 7.4), with --threads=1: 378 mutants, 370 killed,
// 0 errors, 0 syntax errors, 6 time-outs (the loop over the pages of the dead letter stream made endless, and
// five mutants of the condition of the blocking read of RedisStreamsSource::readNew(), which make a receive
// without wait block without end, `BLOCK 0`), 2 escaped, both equivalent:
// - RedisStreamsSource::addClaimed(): the COUNT 1 of `XPENDING <stream> <group> <id> <id> 1` turned into 2; the
//   range holds one entry id, so any count of at least 1 answers the same;
// - RedisStreamsSource::claimReady(): the minimum idle time 0 of the XCLAIM of the deliveries given back turned
//   into -1, which Redis reads as 0.
// MSI 99.47%, covered-code MSI 99.47%, mutation code coverage 100%. The minimum scores are one integer point
// below.
// The workflow runs with one thread too. With --threads=max the score reads higher and is less exact: the blocks of the documentation
// that talk to Redis (DocumentationBlocksTest) share the keys of the default prefix `aspec`, so two processes
// running them at once can fail each other and kill a mutant by that race (the run of 1.0.1 gave 376 killed,
// 1 time-out and 1 escaped, MSI 99.74%). The one it left is the minimum idle time 0 of that XCLAIM turned into
// 1 ms, which differs only when the rejection and the next receive fall in the same millisecond of the server:
// testADeliveryGivenBackComesAgainAtOnce tries that a hundred times in a row and kills it on a machine at
// rest, as the run with one thread did, but cannot force it under the load of a parallel run.
{
    "$schema": "vendor/infection/infection/resources/schema.json",
    "source": {
        "directories": ["src"]
    },
    "timeout": 60,
    "logs": {
        "text": "coverage/infection/infection.log",
        "summary": "coverage/infection/summary.log",
        "json": "coverage/infection/infection.json",
        "perMutator": "coverage/infection/per-mutator.md"
    },
    "tmpDir": "coverage/infection/tmp",
    "phpUnit": {
        "configDir": "."
    },
    "minMsi": 98,
    "minCoveredMsi": 98,
    "mutators": {
        "@default": true
    }
}
